<title>UK: Shell signs for Iraqi crude under oil-for-food dea.</title>
<headline>Shell signs for Iraqi crude under oil-for-food dea.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell Group has signed a contract with Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) to purchase crude under the UN's oil-for-food exchange, a Shell spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The contract has still to be approved by the United Nations.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman declined comment on the volume or time period of the contract.</p>
<p>Iraq has permission to sell $2 billion worth of crude over six months.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
